  "limitations": "Three new acquisitions at each of five commands, same stationary shoe placement; no registration, refitting or bias correction. Object was moved BEFORE this session; old shoe data excluded from repeatability. Same image row across repeats identifies a sampling ray, not independently tracked physical material. Depth variation includes servo, stripe detector and scene effects. Fixed command planes retain known calibration errors. Row SD uses n=3 acquisitions and ddof1; many correlated rows are not extra repeats. Common-row selection can favour reliably detectable areas; report support counts too. Events use two50ms transition windows; APS pools selected lit35ms frames, so this is not equal integration-time, speed, latency or photon-budget comparison. The image-row ROI includes possible background/target crossings after shoe repositioning; interpret as scene-stripe repeatability, not isolated shoe accuracy. Some model-derived APS depths fall outside training ranges; counts retained and reported, no depth filtering. No independent absolute accuracy or full-surface completeness. Temporal scene stability diagnostic is not rigid-body proof."
